# Mutation plan for `api4/user.go`'s two literal-path reads — `GET /api/v4/users/auth_data` and
# `GET /api/v4/users/invalid_emails`.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/user-lookups.plan
#
# **Two suites, and the split is forced.** `/users/invalid_emails` answers 400 whenever
# `TeamSettings.EnableOpenServer` is on, and the stack's Go server pins it on through the
# environment — so the 200 path has no cross-server comparison and its query is tested against
# planted rows in `mm-store`'s `db_users_invalid_emails`. Every mutation to the SQL therefore runs
# under `store`, and only the handler, app and config mutations run under `api`.
#
# `error-body-is-not-html-escaped` is the widest one here: `ApiError::into_wire` now marshals with
# Go's HTML escaping, which every error body on every route goes through. It is catchable only
# because this route's id is `model.NoTranslation` — the literal `<untranslated>` — and no other
# ported route has ever put an angle bracket in an error body.

